invariant: INV-14
file: srv_flight.c
catches: srv_flight_test
reason: srv_select drops the term that reads SRV_EXT_ALPN, so it refuses a
  ClientHello that sent no application_layer_protocol_negotiation extension
  at all. alpn_selected is CH_ALPN_NONE for that hello and for one whose
  list missed, and the seen bit is the only thing that tells them apart, so
  the edit turns every non-ALPN client into a no_application_protocol alert
  against a caller that offers protocols. RFC 7301 section 3.2 makes the
  alert an answer to a list the client sent, not to silence.
  test/srv_flight_tests.h, test_flight_alpn, requires that hello to
  negotiate.

--- old
    return cfg->alpn_count != 0 && (ch->seen & SRV_EXT_ALPN) != 0 &&
           ch->alpn_selected == CH_ALPN_NONE;
--- new
    return cfg->alpn_count != 0 && ch->alpn_selected == CH_ALPN_NONE;
